  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}\u226b{x}^{5}$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{5}}=\\infty .\n$$",
